From c0d917c23687a923583e2ae6331d637f7174103e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 13:57:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(chatbot): repair AI assistant answers, cross-case logic,
 LLM integration and error handling

Backend
- Resolve cases by real case number (#4471 / "case 2" / TRX-style) instead of treating
  "#4472" as DB id 4472; a named case overrides the open case, unknown refs are reported.
- Cross-case links were stored only on the newer case, so the older case reported "no
  overlaps". Match on (type, value) so both directions are found.
- Stop fabricating data: unscored cases no longer get "85/100 HIGH"; scam-trend answer is
  computed from the DB instead of static text; stats include an "awaiting scoring" bucket.
- Fix intent routing (e.g. "explain"/"who" hijacking answers) and answer general questions
  even while a case is open. Add cross-case comparison, shared-entity, highest-risk,
  district, awaiting-scoring and indicator lookup ("where does <number/UPI> appear?").
- Connections view no longer renders empty when a link points at another case's entity.
- Add optional LLM path (reuses AI_SUMMARY_*) with grounded prompt, bounded/sanitised
  context, prompt-injection guard, history support and AI_CHAT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS. Any
  timeout / 4xx / 5xx / malformed reply falls back to data-driven answer with a note.
- Route: input validation (400 with readable detail), friendly response instead of 500,
  new response fields case_number + source (backward compatible).

Frontend (ChatWidget)
- Render **bold**, *italic*, `code` and bullets safely (no innerHTML); show the
  assistant's suggested follow-ups (previously returned but never displayed).
- 30s request timeout with AbortController; specific, readable error messages
  (network / timeout / 4xx / 5xx) instead of one generic string.
- Show case number in header/placeholder instead of DB id; send recent history.
- Position, styling and Standard/Analysis modes unchanged.

Tests: add backend/tests/test_chat_assistant.py (35 tests: routing, accuracy vs DB,
cross-case, LLM success/timeout/401/429/500/bad payload/unconfigured, error handling).
